{"uid":"d671d9adfa3bd4a6","name":"test_a_normalised_fail_inherits_the_all_residual_recomputation","fullName":"tests.test_contract_ladder#test_a_normalised_fail_inherits_the_all_residual_recomputation","historyId":"761782f002a3014f8d34e6e7e92dac34","time":{"start":1791969048219,"stop":1791969048241,"duration":22},"description":"GH #209 defect 2 (Half B): the exact boundary of the node above, and\n    a stated decision rather than a surprise. \"One-directional\" is a\n    property of the MAP, not a promise about the run's outcome: a rewritten\n    payload then receives precisely the treatment a LITERAL `rejected`\n    receives, and that includes `_review_verdict`'s recorded correction of\n    an over-cautious refusal -- a `rejected` claim whose structured findings\n    are ALL `severity: \"residual\"` is recomputed to `verified` (task 002's\n    DoD predicate 3, witnessed by `review.verdict_recomputed`). So a hat\n    that writes `fail` while filing only residual findings does reach\n    `succeeded`, by that route, on its own findings, exactly as it would\n    have with the compliant word.\n\n    Pinned deliberately, in both directions: making `fail` BINDING where\n    `rejected` is correctable would give the contract a second, undeclared\n    verdict vocabulary in which the illegal word outranks the legal one, and\n    silently dropping the recomputation for a normalised payload would be\n    that change made by accident.","descriptionHtml":"<p>GH #209 defect 2 (Half B): the exact boundary of the node above, and<br />\na stated decision rather than a surprise. &quot;One-directional&quot; is a<br />\nproperty of the MAP, not a promise about the run's outcome: a rewritten<br />\npayload then receives precisely the treatment a LITERAL <code>rejected</code><br />\nreceives, and that includes <code>_review_verdict</code>'s recorded correction of<br />\nan over-cautious refusal -- a <code>rejected</code> claim whose structured findings<br />\nare ALL <code>severity: &quot;residual&quot;</code> is recomputed to <code>verified</code> (task 002's<br />\nDoD predicate 3, witnessed by <code>review.verdict_recomputed</code>). So a hat<br />\nthat writes <code>fail</code> while filing only residual findings does reach<br />\n<code>succeeded</code>, by that route, on its own findings, exactly as it would<br />\nhave with the compliant word.</p>\n<pre><code>Pinned deliberately, in both directions: making `fail` BINDING where\n`rejected` is correctable would give the contract a second, undeclared\nverdict vocabulary in which the illegal word outranks the legal one, and\nsilently dropping the recomputation for a normalised payload would be\nthat change made by accident.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791968776884,"stop":1791968776885,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791968776885,"stop":1791968776885,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791969048198,"stop":1791969048198,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791969048198,"stop":1791969048205,"duration":7},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791969048206,"